# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This project currently ships as static HTML/CSS/JS with no
# build step, so there is no tool (webpack/vite/etc.) that
# reads a .env file today. The actual place these two values
# live is js/config.js — a gitignored file you create once from
# js/config.example.js (see README.md → "Configuration").
#
# This file exists so that:
#
#   1. The two values the app needs are documented in one place,
#      independent of whichever config mechanism is in use.
#   2. If a build step is introduced later, switching js/config.js
#      to read from environment variables is a small, contained
#      change — this file is the contract for what those
#      variables should be called.
#
# Copy this file to .env only if/when a build tool that supports
# it is added to the project. Never commit a real .env file.
# See README.md → "Security" for why SUPABASE_KEY is safe to
# expose in client-side code, and why it's still kept out of git
# regardless.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Supabase project URL, e.g. https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Supabase "publishable" (anon) key — NOT the service_role key.
# The service_role key must never appear in any frontend file,
# committed or not.
SUPABASE_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key-here
